meta {
  name: S10.60 C4: the admin filters on description: not masked, 400 field_not_filterable (description is not flagged)
  type: http
  seq: 60
}

get {
  url: {{core_url}}/api/v1/records/incident?filter[description]=s10-internal-{{s10_run}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{admin_a_token}}
}

tests {
  const N = require('./lib/nava')({ test, expect, res, bru });
  N.problem('field_not_filterable', 400);
  N.fieldError('/filter/description');
}

docs {
  The mask admits the admin, so the answer is the registry's, not `masked_field` (S10.56 is Alice's). Since ADR-006 D6 a data filter needs the field flagged `x-nava-filterable`, and `description` is on neither the flag nor the legacy allow-list (`incident.priority` only). The value is unchanged: S10.55 shows the admin reads it. Flagging it needs the P7-05 backfill to reach `ready`; the kit adds that step when it lands.
}
